Z1. HARD AUDIT OF BOTH PROOFS (C AND G)

Audit of C (supermartingale composition):
1. Supermartingale bound (1) and dyadic constant (4A/3)^(2/3): The core probabilistic argument is rigorous and elegant. Conditioning on the stopping time tau_a when the a-th distinct block J_a is opened (1 <= a <= t) makes J_a, its quota d_{J_a} = ceil(3 h_{J_a} / 4), and its sorted size profile lambda_{J_a}(k) measurable before its first credited probe. Because 1 + (e^theta - 1) p_n <= exp((e^theta - 1) p_n), exp(theta Y - (e^theta - 1) P) is a genuine nonnegative supermartingale; setting theta = log(d_j / M_j(t)) when M_j(t) < d_j gives -(e^theta - 1) P >= -d_j + M_j(t) >= -d_j, proving (1). The asymptotic calculus from lambda_j(k) >= A sqrt(x log(k+1)) to c_A = (4A/3)^(2/3) is also exact (A = sqrt(2) gives (32/9)^(1/3) = 1.5263; A = 2 gives (64/9)^(1/3) = 1.9230).
2. Small-quota cusp overflow bug in C: In C's private-field certificate, Lemma FT leaves O(D log(2E)) Farey-cusp exceptions, which C absorbs into floor(h/4) ("if the errors fit the private quota"). However, an adaptive algorithm can open a block with degree D ~ (x / log x)^(1/3), box log E ~ x^(1/3), and a polynomial smoothness bound B = x^(1/2) (so mu = (1/2) log x and h ~ x^(1/2) / log x). Then D log(2E) ~ x^(2/3) >> floor(h/4) ~ x^(1/2), so the cusp exceptions overflow floor(h/4) and hypothesis (2) fails for small-h blocks unless either h >= C_0 D log(2E) is enforced or cusp points are not granted as free automatic successes. (Similarly, C2's Davenport error O(DE) overflows floor(h/4) whenever E > B / D.)
3. Gaming C's sharing/credit rules and failure to imply GNFS/MNFS bounds: MAJOR GAP. C allows first-stage shared rational tests g(a, b) = a - b m to run as uncredited work, requiring credited blocks only on the private algebraic forms f_v(a, b) ("Grant all rational survivors"). This breaks tightness and even positivity on proved inputs:
  (a) On two-stage SNFS (N = r^e - 2, g = a - b m uncredited, f = a^d - 2 b^d credited), |disc(f)| = d^d 2^(d-1) is independent of N, so xi = 0 in C's private-field certificate! Because C's theorem bounds W only by credited probes t / S and ignores uncredited work W_0, C's proved certificate gives A = sqrt(xi) = 0 (c_A = 0, vacuous) on two-stage SNFS.
  (b) Even on ordinary two-stage GNFS (g tested first uncredited, f credited on survivors), f alone has heuristic norm x/D + (D/2) log k (A = sqrt(2), constant 1.5263, NOT 1.9230), and on MNFS/Factory C's theorem yields at best 1.5263 heuristically—never 1.9019 or 1.6386 (C's final section only checks that the classical MNFS cost formula optimizes to 1.9019; C's lower bound does not prove 1.9019).
  (c) Even for one-stage joint GNFS, C's proved C2/FT input uses only N^2 | disc(g f), giving A = sqrt(2) (1.5263); reaching A = 2 (1.9230) requires Theorem GAE plus typical/full-box norm dominance, not proved sublevel area alone.

Audit of G (model M_G and Step 2):
1. Step 2 (removing Assumption T via B_* = T^2 (log N)^C and t_last): Two real bugs are fixable; a third is structural:
  (a) Giant-box / forced-modulus prime blowup (FIXABLE): G's D2 allowed doubly-subexponential boxes log E_t <= B_t / (16 D_m) and uncapped polynomial heights, so one earlier step t_1 or forced modulus M_1 could create Omega(T) primes > B_*, ruining the O(T^2 / B_*) SM2 birthday bound. Fix: measure T in bit operations (as C does), forcing sum_{t <= T} log_2 |W(a_t)| <= T so at most T primes > B_* ever appear (forced or unforced) in the entire transcript.
  (b) Forced-times-unforced even valuation at t_last (FIXABLE): G stated SM2 only for p not dividing N(M_t). If p > B_* has p || M_{t_last} (forced) and p || C_{t_last} (unforced), then v_p(W) = 2 is even, escaping L_+ while leaving p | C_{t_last}. Fix: apply SM2 to the stripped cofactor C_t for ALL p > B (including p | M_t), union-bounded across the <= T active primes by T^2 D (log N)^(O(1)) / B_* = o(1).
  (c) Sublattice Farey cusps at single step t_last (STRUCTURAL): Applying FT to G = (W o M_{t_last}) / Q leaves O(D log E_Q) cusp exceptions on Lambda_Q. Contrary to G's claim, H_sel does NOT suppress them when E >= sqrt(Q) (E_Q >= 1), because an algorithm can deterministically compute continued-fraction convergents of M^(-1)(theta_i). Because Step 2 isolates only ONE step t_last (unlike Step 3's h >> D log E quota), one lucky Liouville cusp hit on G is not absorbed by quota h. Thus Assumption-T removal requires an explicit non-cusp cofactor hypothesis on Lambda_Q (whereas keeping Assumption T gives >= d_j distinct terminal leaves, absorbing O(D log E_Q) exceptions whenever d_j >> D log E_Q).
2. Constants, batch union bound, and Axiom NP:
  - Constants (k/18)^(1/3) (0.3816, 0.4807), special-N floors 1.2114 / 1.5263, and free-LA (omega = 0) floors 1.8595 (MNFS) and 1.6363 (Factory) are algebraically exact: e.g. 2e - sqrt(2ke)/(3b) >= b with 3b(2e - b) <= 3e^2 gives (2e)^3 >= 16k/9 with zero LA cost, and in MNFS at omega = 0, 2e = 2e - r_0 + v binds at 1.859536.
  - Batch union bound flaw: G's Step 1 union bound (T K <= N^(1-eps)) assumed norms W were generated independently of the batch; what actually prevented cross-target routing in M_G was D2's syntactic pre-assignment of one target j_t per probe.
  - Axiom NP omission (FIXABLE): G wrote "order-index scalars away from Res", omitting gcd(disc W_m, N_j) in {1, N_j}. Without that, f_1 = x^2 + 1, f_2 = (x - delta)^2 + 1 with q_j | delta, p_j not dividing delta has gcd(Res, N_j) = q_j, halving N^2 | disc to q_j^2 ~ N. Fix: require gcd(disc W_m, N_j) in {1, N_j}.


Z2. ADVERSARY A1 AND THE EXACT BATCH CAP

Adversary A1 is valid as a pure relation-collection RAM algorithm, with two minor refinements: (i) use U_0 subset [2N, 4N] (instead of [2N, 5N/2]) so binary-doubling prefixes guarantees O(log N) worst-case delay per smooth output; note gcd(u, N_j) = 1 holds automatically for balanced semiprimes and distinct pairs (u, v) with u - v = N_j never share u/v (since u v' = u' v implies (u - v)/(u' - v') = 1); (ii) at B = (log N)^3, equidistribution of smooth differences u - v across semiprimes in [N, 2N) is heuristic (plus R), whereas raising B to L_N[1/4, 1] still beats L_N[1/3] with analytical dispersion support.

Exact batch caps (for K distinct i.i.d. random semiprimes in [N, 2N)):
- Pure relation collection (no gcd splits): K <= N^(1 - eps) is the sharp cap. Any W target-blind nonzero integers <= 2^W have <= tau(.) = N^(o(1)) divisors in [N, 2N), so hitting Omega(K) random targets requires W >= N^(1 - o(1)), forcing W / K >= N^(eps - o(1)) >> L_N[1/3]. Above K = N / L_N[1/3], A1 beats L_N[1/3].
- Allowing batch gcd / remainder-tree splitting: K <= N^(1/2 - eps) is the sharp cap, because Bernstein's remainder-tree trial division takes O~(N^(1/2) + K) bit operations, beating L_N[1/3] per target once K >= N^(1/2) / L_N[1/3].
- Inside C's pre-revelation credit model (sum Q_i <= e^(o(F)) W and known smooth factors stripped so A1 has residual size s = 0): no size cap on K is needed once targets are distinct and pairwise coprime, because A1 violates both residual-size positivity and pre-revelation target registration.


Z3. MERGED THEOREM CG (UNIFIED ADAPTIVE RELATION-COLLECTION LOWER BOUND)

Model M_CG (Bit-Charged Filtered Linked-Valuation Model):
Input: K distinct, pairwise coprime odd composites N_1, ..., N_K in [N, 2N) (with 1 <= K <= N^(1/2 - eps) if untargeted differences/gcds are allowed). Execution is a uniform randomized RAM/DAG of total bit-work W (so sum_{probes} log_2 |norm| <= W).
- [MODEL-ASSUMPTION NP]: Every registered presentation P_m = (A_m, M_m, psi_m) for N_j splits A_m into Q-irreducible fields K_{m,l}, satisfies gcd(v, N_j) in {1, N_j} on all Q-idempotents, generator denominators, and disc(W_m) (so Lemma ND/CC PROVES N_j^(k_m) | disc(W_m) with k_m = 2 ring-map, k_m = 1 ramified, and pairwise N_j | Res(f_u, f_v)), and receives <= O(log log N) external non-splitting advice bits.
- Two-Tier Block Credits: Blocks (target j, field/pair set, bound B = e^mu, quota h >= 1) are opened before their first credited probe; known divisors M_t are stripped first. Shared Stage-0 blocks (N_j-independent, e.g. rational a - b m) pay work W_0 >= t_0 once globally and pass at most S_0 smooth survivors to Stage-1 partner blocks f_v; target-credited probes satisfy sum_{j=1}^K Q_j <= e^(o(F_{1/3})) W. Sparse F_2 LA on S active columns costs S^omega (omega in [0, 2]).
- [HEURISTICS SM1, SM2, H_sel, R]: Conditional on F_{t-1}, fresh stripped cofactors C_t satisfy Pr[C_t B-smooth] <= rho(log C_t / mu)^(1 - o(1)) (SM1); for all primes p > B, Pr[p | C_t and v_p(C_t) odd, or p^2 | C_t] <= D (log N)^(O(1)) / p (SM2); lattices with Q = N(M_t) > (2E)^r obey E[#new primitive points] <= O((2E)^r / Q) (H_sel). Extraction for N_j requires a nonempty F_2-dependency D_j where each active field K_v below scale B_v contributes R_v >= B_v^(1 - o(1)) rows (and shared base K_0 requires sum_v R_v >= B_0^(1 - o(1))) with log h >= (1 - o(1)) mu (R).

Arithmetic Profile Inputs:
- [PROVED]: Rank-2 pairs (g, f_v) satisfy lambda(k) >= k_m x / (2(D-1)) + (D/2) log(k / 16) after O(D log(2E)) Farey-cusp exceptions (Bean + Lemma FT); rank r >= 3 GP/framed modules satisfy the Bean-Thunder/FH bound when (2E)^(r-1) <= h / (16 r D); reduced KH modules in the theta-regular subclass satisfy lambda(k) >= (theta / sqrt(7)) sqrt(x log(k+1)).
- [MODEL-ASSUMPTION]: LP_exc^rel (degenerate/large-box rank r >= 3 modulo O_k^x and proper subspaces); H_cusp (non-Liouville cofactor separation on single descent sublattices Lambda_Q when dropping Assumption T, or small-quota blocks h <= O(D log E)); GAE-norm (for 1 - o(1) of N, examined boxes achieve the GAE base-m height floor eta_0, eta_v >= 1/d).

Theorem CG [MODEL-PROVED in M_CG]:
To solve >= delta K targets in expectation (fixed delta > 0):
1. All-N Universal Floor (omega = 0): Applying C's supermartingale (1) to both Stage-0 and paired (g, f_v) blocks (pairing at most one low-discriminant field f_{v*} with g and bounding the remaining V - 1 fields by pairwise N_j | Res(f_u, f_v)), if all active primes lie <= B_* = W^2 (log N)^C (or under tree-incidence T with d_j >> D log E_Q), E[W]/K >= L_N[1/3, (16/9)^(1/3) = 1.2114] (k = 1) and L_N[1/3, (32/9)^(1/3) = 1.5263] (k = 2, SNFS-tight). Without Assumption T, if D_j uses primes > B_*, Step 2 under H_cusp gives E[W] >= L_N[1/3, (k/18)^(1/3)] (0.3816 / 0.4807).
2. Generic Tight MNFS & Factory Floors (i.i.d. targets in [N_0, 2N_0) under GAE-norm):
   For K = 1, E[W] >= L_N[1/3, 1.9019] at omega = 2 (1.8595 at omega = 0). For 1 <= K <= N^(1/2 - eps), E[W] >= max(L_N[1/3, 1.9019], K * L_N[1/3, 1.6386]) at omega = 2 (1.6363 at omega = 0).


Z4. TOP 3 HOSTILE-REFEREE ATTACKS (AND FIXABILITY)

1. Point-probe pricing (SM1 + H_sel) assumes away beyond-Johnson CRT decoders (M2) and Prop SI constructors: Because O~(B) public residues mod q^(e_q) uniquely determine all smooth box points, a referee will note the theorem bounds sieving/probe algorithms, not arbitrary circuits on public syndromes. Fixability: Unfixable unconditionally (needs superpolynomial circuit lower bounds); completely fixable in presentation by naming M_CG a "priced valuation-probe model" and citing Theorem J for oblivious Johnson decoders.
2. Cusp exceptions overflowing tiny quotas (h <= O(D log E)) or single-step t_last descent (H_cusp): A referee will test B = poly(log N) on D ~ x^(1/3) where D log E >> h, or deterministic continued-fraction hits on Lambda_Q in Step 2. Fixability: Fixable for tiny-B blocks via Bombieri-Schmidt / Thue-Mahler bounds (irreducible degree-D forms have O(D s^r) solutions to B-smooth Thue-Mahler equations when log B = O(log x), or small D forces log|W| = Omega(x) by Liouville); for Step 2 without Assumption T, requires keeping H_cusp or effective subspace/Roth bounds.
3. GAE height-to-area gap (1.5263 vs 1.9019) and LP_exc^rel / R: A referee will point out that GAE bounds polynomial heights while C2/FT bound SL_2(R)-invariant area (so thin skewed sub-boxes could in principle mimic SNFS's 1.5263 on generic N), and unit cones O_k^x at r >= 3 or short structured F_2-cycles remain open. Fixability: The 1.2114 / 1.5263 all-N rank-2 floors are ALREADY immune to the GAE-area gap; closing 1.5263 -> 1.9019 without GAE-norm requires counting SL_2(Z)-equivalence classes of small-discriminant forms divisible by N (hard for D >= 4), while LP_exc^rel and R remain genuine open arithmetic conjectures.
